{"l":8320,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The coach did not shout after the defeat. He simply asked each player to write down one thing they could have done better.' Hvad kendetegner trænerens reaktion?","o":["Han er skuffet og vil helst give op nu","Han er vred og vil straffe hele holdet","Han er ligeglad med, hvordan det gik","Han er rolig og vil have dem til at lære"],"a":"Han er rolig og vil have dem til at lære","r":"Han råber ikke, men beder spillerne om at tænke over, hvad de kan forbedre."},
{"l":8340,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Oliver's grandmother learned to use a tablet at 85. Now she sends the family photos every morning and corrects their spelling in the group chat.' Hvordan beskrives bedstemoren?","o":["Som nysgerrig og aktiv","Som træt og gammeldags","Som streng og vred","Som glemsom og forvirret"],"a":"Som nysgerrig og aktiv","r":"Hun lærte noget nyt som 85-årig og bruger det hver dag. Hun er nysgerrig og aktiv."},
{"l":8365,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Jakob had always laughed at people who ran marathons. Last Sunday, his family cheered as he crossed the finish line.' Hvad viser teksten?","o":["Jakob griner stadig af løbere","Jakob har ændret holdning","Jakob så på et maraton","Jakob gav op undervejs"],"a":"Jakob har ændret holdning","r":"Han grinede før af maratonløbere, men nu har han selv løbet et. Han har altså skiftet mening."},
{"l":8405,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'It's time we ___ home; it's getting dark.'","o":["go","will go","went","have gone"],"a":"went","r":"Efter 'It's time we' bruger man datid, selv om det handler om nu."},
{"l":8430,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man vil bede om at få en nat til at tænke over et tilbud?","o":["Can I sleep over it?","May I think it on?","Can I dream about it?","Can I sleep on it?"],"a":"Can I sleep on it?","r":"'Sleep on it' betyder at vente til næste dag med at beslutte sig."},
{"l":8470,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'pull their weight' i 'Everyone in the group has to pull their weight'?","o":["gøre deres del","tabe sig","løfte tunge ting","bestemme det hele"],"a":"gøre deres del","r":"'Pull your weight' betyder at gøre sin del af arbejdet i en gruppe."},
{"l":8495,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The volunteers spent the whole weekend cleaning the beach. On Monday, a storm washed up just as much rubbish again, but they simply arranged another weekend.' Hvad kendetegner de frivillige?","o":["De giver hurtigt op","De er vedholdende","De er ligeglade","De er utålmodige"],"a":"De er vedholdende","r":"De lader sig ikke slå ud af stormen, men planlægger bare en ny weekend."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'i sidste ende' på engelsk i '___, it's your decision'?","o":["previously","currently","ultimately","occasionally"],"a":"ultimately","r":"'Ultimately' = i sidste ende."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'resultat' på engelsk?","o":["income","outline","outlook","outcome"],"a":"outcome","r":"'Outcome' betyder resultatet af noget."},
{"l":8510,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'arid' i 'an arid region'?","o":["dry","cold","hilly","remote"],"a":"dry","r":"'Arid' betyder meget tør, typisk om et område med næsten ingen regn."},
{"l":8520,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The new sports hall was finished on time and on budget, which, for this council, is something of a miracle.' Hvad antyder skribenten om kommunen?","o":["At kommunen altid bygger flotte sportshaller","At kommunen sjældent holder tid og budget","At kommunen har fået mange flere penge","At kommunen ikke interesserer sig for sport"],"a":"At kommunen sjældent holder tid og budget","r":"'Something of a miracle' er ironisk: det er usædvanligt, at netop denne kommune overholder tid og budget."},
{"l":8540,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'It's no use ___ about the weather; we can't change it.'","o":["to complain","complain","complaining","complained"],"a":"complaining","r":"Efter 'It's no use' bruges ing-form: 'It's no use complaining'."},
{"l":8560,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Her speech left a lasting ___ on the audience.'","o":["expression","oppression","depression","impression"],"a":"impression","r":"'Leave a lasting impression' betyder at gøre et varigt indtryk."},
{"l":8580,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'vigilant' i 'remain vigilant'?","o":["watchful","patient","silent","hopeful"],"a":"watchful","r":"'Vigilant' betyder årvågen og opmærksom, altså 'watchful'."},
{"l":8600,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'ardent' i 'an ardent supporter'?","o":["occasional","passionate","former","quiet"],"a":"passionate","r":"'Ardent' betyder ivrig og brændende engageret, altså 'passionate'."},
{"l":8620,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'lucid' i 'a lucid explanation'?","o":["lengthy","polite","clear","sudden"],"a":"clear","r":"'Lucid' betyder klar og let at forstå, altså 'clear'."},
{"l":8650,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Not only ___ the exam, but she also got the highest mark in the class.'","o":["she passed","passed she","she did pass","did she pass"],"a":"did she pass","r":"Efter 'Not only' først i sætningen bruges omvendt ordstilling med hjælpeverbum: 'did she pass'."},
{"l":8680,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Tom rolled his eyes and said that he simply adored spending his Saturdays cleaning out the garage.' Hvordan skal Toms udsagn forstås?","o":["Som ironi: han bryder sig ikke om det","Som et ærligt udtryk for glæde","Som et tilbud om at hjælpe andre","Som en klage over sin far"],"a":"Som ironi: han bryder sig ikke om det","r":"At han himler med øjnene ('rolled his eyes') viser, at 'simply adored' er ironisk ment."},
{"l":8700,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man høfligt vil afbryde nogen i en diskussion for at sige noget?","o":["Excuse me, can I take the word now?","Sorry to interrupt, but may I add something?","Stop talking, it is my turn to speak.","Pardon me, may I break in your talk?"],"a":"Sorry to interrupt, but may I add something?","r":"'Sorry to interrupt, but ...' er en høflig måde at afbryde på. 'Take the word' er en direkte oversættelse fra dansk og bruges ikke."},
{"l":8720,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: '___ in 1888, the school is one of the oldest in the region.'","o":["Founding","Being founding","Founded","Having founded"],"a":"Founded","r":"Skolen blev grundlagt, så det er en passiv participiumsætning: 'Founded in 1888'."},
{"l":8750,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man høfligt vil sige, at man er uenig med nogen i et møde?","o":["I am totally disagree with you about it.","You are just wrong about this, full stop.","I don't agree you about this at all.","I see your point, but I see it differently."],"a":"I see your point, but I see it differently.","r":"'I see your point, but ...' anerkender den andens synspunkt og er høflig. 'I am disagree' og 'agree you' er grammatisk forkerte."},
{"l":8780,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'hostile' i 'a hostile reception'?","o":["warm","noisy","brief","formal"],"a":"warm","r":"'Hostile' betyder fjendtlig, så det modsatte er en 'warm' (venlig, hjertelig) modtagelse."},
{"l":8810,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'It was only when the lights went out ___ we realised the storm was serious.'","o":["which","that","what","who"],"a":"that","r":"Kløvet sætning: 'It was ... that ...' fremhæver tidspunktet. 'Which' og 'what' kan ikke bruges i denne konstruktion."},
{"l":8830,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'frail' i 'a frail old man'?","o":["grumpy","wealthy","weak","wise"],"a":"weak","r":"'Frail' betyder svagelig og skrøbelig, altså 'weak'."},
{"l":8860,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'I don't like horror films, and neither ___ my best friend.'","o":["likes","doesn't","is","does"],"a":"does","r":"Efter 'neither' bruges inversion med et bekræftende hjælpeverbum: 'neither does my best friend'. 'Doesn't' ville give dobbelt nægtelse."},
{"l":8900,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'She said she would finish the essay by Friday, and she ___.'","o":["did","made","was","got"],"a":"did","r":"'Did' erstatter hele udsagnet 'finished the essay by Friday' (substitution), så man undgår gentagelse."},
{"l":8940,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The museum is, admittedly, not the largest in the country, but what it lacks in size it more than makes up for in charm.' Hvad mener skribenten om museet?","o":["Stort, men lidt kedeligt","Lille, men meget charmerende","Hverken stort eller charmerende","Landets største og flotteste"],"a":"Lille, men meget charmerende","r":"'What it lacks in size it more than makes up for in charm' betyder, at charmen mere end opvejer den lille størrelse."},
{"l":8980,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man vil bede nogen om ikke at presse én til at beslutte sig hurtigt?","o":["Don't hurry on me.","Don't stress me up.","Don't rush me.","Don't push me over."],"a":"Don't rush me.","r":"'Don't rush me' betyder 'lad være med at skynde på mig'. 'Push me over' betyder at skubbe én omkuld."},
{"l":8996,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'altafgørende' på engelsk?","o":["tantamount","paranoid","peripheral","paramount"],"a":"paramount","r":"'Paramount' = vigtigst af alt."},
{"l":9000,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'We regret to inform you that your application has not been successful on this occasion. We wish you every success in the future.' Hvilken tone har teksten?","o":["Høflig og formel","Vred og anklagende","Spøgefuld og personlig","Begejstret og glad"],"a":"Høflig og formel","r":"'We regret to inform you' og 'We wish you every success' er faste, høflige og formelle vendinger i et afslag."},
{"l":9010,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'hindered' i 'The heavy backpack hindered his progress up the hill.'?","o":["hjalp","hæmmede","målte","viste"],"a":"hæmmede","r":"'Hinder' betyder at hæmme eller hindre; den tunge rygsæk gjorde det sværere at komme op."},
{"l":9020,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Scarcely ___ the house when it started to snow.'","o":["we had left","have we left","had we left","we have left"],"a":"had we left","r":"'Scarcely' først i sætningen kræver inversion, og mønstret er 'Scarcely had ... when ...' med førnutid."},
{"l":9031,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'ambitiøs' på engelsk?","o":["ambiguous","auspicious","cautious","ambitious"],"a":"ambitious","r":"'Ambitious' betyder ambitiøs eller ærgerrig."},
{"l":9040,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Scientists hope the new telescope will ___ light on how galaxies form.'","o":["shed","put","bring","take"],"a":"shed","r":"Den faste forbindelse er 'shed light on' (kaste lys over). De andre verber danner ikke et udtryk med 'light on'."},
{"l":9043,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'partiskhed / skævvridning' på engelsk i 'The article showed a clear political ___'?","o":["basis","bias","shift","debate"],"a":"bias","r":"'Bias' = forudindtagethed."},
{"l":9052,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'medgørlig / følger reglerne' på engelsk?","o":["complacent","competent","compliant","compatible"],"a":"compliant","r":"'Compliant' betyder, at man følger regler eller krav."},
{"l":9060,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'a tall order' i 'Finishing the whole project by Monday is a tall order.'?","o":["en stor bestilling","en høj bygning","en klar besked","en svær opgave"],"a":"en svær opgave","r":"'A tall order' er en opgave, der er meget svær eller næsten umulig at klare."},
{"l":9066,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'snu / skarpsindig' på engelsk?","o":["shrewd","shrill","crude","stern"],"a":"shrewd","r":"'Shrewd' = snu, kløgtig."},
{"l":9077,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'stædig' på engelsk?","o":["obsolete","obstinate","obedient","fortunate"],"a":"obstinate","r":"'Obstinate' = stædig."},
{"l":9088,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'overfladisk' på engelsk?","o":["superfluous","artificial","superficial","beneficial"],"a":"superficial","r":"'Superficial' betyder overfladisk."},
{"l":9090,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'curb' i 'The town wants to curb traffic near the school.'?","o":["overvåge","omdirigere","fremme","begrænse"],"a":"begrænse","r":"'Curb' betyder at begrænse eller holde noget i tømme."},
{"l":9101,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'betydelig / væsentlig' på engelsk?","o":["substantial","substandard","sequential","influential"],"a":"substantial","r":"'Substantial' = betydelig."},
{"l":9110,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'All I wanted ___ a quiet evening with a good book.'","o":["were","was","has","did"],"a":"was","r":"'All I wanted' fungerer som ental-subjekt i en kløvet sætning, så verbet er 'was'."},
{"l":9112,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'ubetydelig' på engelsk?","o":["negligent","eligible","negligible","legible"],"a":"negligible","r":"'Negligible' = så lille, at man kan se bort fra det."},
{"l":9125,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'uden fortilfælde' på engelsk?","o":["unpredictable","unsupervised","unprotected","unprecedented"],"a":"unprecedented","r":"'Unprecedented' betyder, at det aldrig er sket før."},
{"l":9136,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'udbredt' på engelsk?","o":["prevalent","relevant","prudent","prominent"],"a":"prevalent","r":"'Prevalent' = udbredt."},
{"l":9147,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'fattig / nødlidende' på engelsk?","o":["resolute","destitute","desolate","obstinate"],"a":"destitute","r":"'Destitute' = uden midler."},
{"l":9150,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'misforståelse' på engelsk i 'It is a common ___ that bats are blind.'?","o":["misbehaviour","mischief","misconception","misfortune"],"a":"misconception","r":"'Misconception' er en udbredt, forkert opfattelse. 'Misfortune' er uheld, og 'mischief' er ballade."},
{"l":9160,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'come rain or shine' i 'We train every Tuesday, come rain or shine.'?","o":["kun i solskin","kun når det regner","om foråret","uanset vejret"],"a":"uanset vejret","r":"'Come rain or shine' betyder uanset vejret eller uanset hvad."},
{"l":9170,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'empirisk / baseret på observation' på engelsk?","o":["empirical","imperial","theoretical","emotional"],"a":"empirical","r":"'Empirical' = baseret på erfaring og data."},
{"l":9180,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'cut him some slack' i 'He is new here, so cut him some slack.'?","o":["giv ham mindre arbejde","vær lidt overbærende med ham","gør grin med ham","hold øje med ham"],"a":"vær lidt overbærende med ham","r":"'Cut someone some slack' betyder at være overbærende og ikke for streng over for nogen."},
{"l":9182,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'kortvarig / flygtig' på engelsk?","o":["empirical","peripheral","ephemeral","perennial"],"a":"ephemeral","r":"'Ephemeral' = flygtig."},
{"l":9194,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'afvigelse' på engelsk?","o":["analogy","anatomy","autonomy","anomaly"],"a":"anomaly","r":"'Anomaly' = noget unormalt."},
{"l":9200,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Not ___ what to say, she simply smiled and nodded.'","o":["knowing","known","to know","knew"],"a":"knowing","r":"'Not knowing what to say' er en nægtende participiumsætning, der forklarer årsagen til, at hun smilede."},
{"l":9210,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'underforstået' på engelsk?","o":["explicit","implicit","illicit","intrinsic"],"a":"implicit","r":"'Implicit' betyder underforstået. Det modsatte er 'explicit'."},
{"l":9217,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'årsagssammenhæng' på engelsk?","o":["cessation","location","causation","sensation"],"a":"causation","r":"'Causation' = at én ting forårsager en anden."},
{"l":9228,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'paradoks / selvmodsigelse' på engelsk?","o":["parody","paradigm","parable","paradox"],"a":"paradox","r":"'Paradox' = noget tilsyneladende selvmodsigende."},
{"l":9240,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'indre / iboende' på engelsk?","o":["intrinsic","intricate","extrinsic","intrusive"],"a":"intrinsic","r":"'Intrinsic' = indre, iboende."},
{"l":9240,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man i et formelt møde vil bede nogen om at gentage det sidste, de sagde?","o":["Huh, what was that you just said there?","Sorry, could you repeat that last point?","Repeat the last thing you said again.","Could you say me that last point again?"],"a":"Sorry, could you repeat that last point?","r":"'Sorry, could you repeat that last point?' er høfligt og korrekt. 'Say me' er forkert, og 'Huh' og en bydeform er for uformelle."},
{"l":9252,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'forlige / forene' på engelsk?","o":["recollect","recline","reconcile","recount"],"a":"reconcile","r":"'Reconcile' = forlige, få til at passe sammen."},
{"l":9260,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The window is broken, so someone ___ have kicked a ball through it.'","o":["should","ought","would","must"],"a":"must","r":"'Must have' + kort tillægsform udtrykker en sikker slutning om fortiden. 'Ought' kræver 'to', og 'should have' betyder burde have."},
{"l":9263,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'modbevise' på engelsk?","o":["refute","refuse","repute","recruit"],"a":"refute","r":"'Refute' = modbevise."},
{"l":9280,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'If he had saved his money, he ___ a new bike now.'","o":["could have afforded","could afford","would have afford","can afford"],"a":"could afford","r":"Blandet betingelse: fortiden ('had saved') påvirker nutiden ('now'), så hovedsætningen er 'could afford'."},
{"l":9290,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'exquisite' i 'The museum displays exquisite jewellery from the Viking Age.'?","o":["billige","tunge","udsøgte","simple"],"a":"udsøgte","r":"'Exquisite' betyder udsøgt og meget smuk og fint udført."},
{"l":9298,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'kortfattet' på engelsk?","o":["concave","conscious","coarse","concise"],"a":"concise","r":"'Concise' betyder kort og præcis i formen."},
{"l":9310,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'afskrække' på engelsk?","o":["deter","defer","detect","decay"],"a":"deter","r":"'Deter' = afskrække."},
{"l":9310,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Can you join us for lunch? I'd love ___, but I have a dentist appointment.'","o":["it","to","so","that"],"a":"to","r":"Ellipse: 'I'd love to' står for 'I'd love to join you'. 'To' alene erstatter resten af infinitiven."},
{"l":9321,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'forståelig' på engelsk?","o":["comprehensive","compatible","comprehensible","contemptible"],"a":"comprehensible","r":"'Comprehensible' betyder forståelig."},
{"l":9332,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'fordømme' på engelsk?","o":["condone","contend","condense","condemn"],"a":"condemn","r":"'Condemn' betyder fordømme."},
{"l":9340,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'sceptical' i 'a sceptical audience'?","o":["convinced","bored","large","noisy"],"a":"convinced","r":"'Sceptical' betyder skeptisk og i tvivl, så det modsatte er 'convinced' (overbevist)."},
{"l":9345,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'stige kraftigt / svæve' på engelsk?","o":["sow","soar","soak","sear"],"a":"soar","r":"'Soar' = stige kraftigt (fx priser)."},
{"l":9356,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'styrtdykke' på engelsk?","o":["pummel","plunder","plummet","flutter"],"a":"plummet","r":"'Plummet' = falde brat."},
{"l":9369,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'diskret' på engelsk?","o":["discrete","distinct","devout","discreet"],"a":"discreet","r":"'Discreet' betyder diskret. 'Discrete' betyder adskilt."},
{"l":9380,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'tilbageslag' på engelsk?","o":["setback","feedback","backlog","outset"],"a":"setback","r":"'Setback' = tilbageslag."},
{"l":9391,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'gentage' på engelsk?","o":["retaliate","reiterate","reinstate","irritate"],"a":"reiterate","r":"'Reiterate' = gentage, understrege igen."},
{"l":9400,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'He ___ to have been a brilliant footballer when he was young.'","o":["says","said","is said","is saying"],"a":"is said","r":"'He is said to have been' er en passiv refererende konstruktion: man siger om ham, at han var en dygtig spiller."},
{"l":9420,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'I would love to come to your party on Saturday. Unfortunately, I have promised to help my aunt move house that day.' Hvad er formålet med teksten?","o":["At sige ja til at komme til festen","At bede om hjælp til en flytning","At invitere vennen med til tanten","At takke høfligt nej til festen"],"a":"At takke høfligt nej til festen","r":"'I would love to ... Unfortunately' er en høflig måde at sige nej på."},
{"l":9450,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The reason ___ I am late is that the bus broke down.'","o":["why","because","for","what"],"a":"why","r":"Konstruktionen er 'The reason why ... is that ...'. 'The reason because' er forkert."},
{"l":9480,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'dormant' i 'a dormant volcano'?","o":["extinct","active","distant","enormous"],"a":"active","r":"'Dormant' betyder slumrende eller hvilende, så det modsatte er 'active'. En 'extinct' vulkan er helt udslukt."},
{"l":9520,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Having spent the entire weekend revising, Sara was somewhat surprised, and more than a little annoyed, to learn that the test had been postponed.' Hvordan har Sara det?","o":["Lettet og meget glad","Helt ligeglad med det","Overrasket og ret irriteret","Nervøs og bange"],"a":"Overrasket og ret irriteret","r":"'More than a little annoyed' er en underdrivelse, der betyder ret irriteret; hun havde jo læst hele weekenden."},
{"l":9550,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'diminutive' i 'a diminutive figure'?","o":["distant","elegant","gloomy","tiny"],"a":"tiny","r":"'Diminutive' betyder meget lille, altså 'tiny'."},
{"l":9570,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The author never tells us directly that Anna is lonely; instead, we see her setting the table for two every evening, although she lives alone.' Hvordan viser forfatteren Annas ensomhed?","o":["Gennem det, hun gør","Gennem en direkte beskrivelse","Gennem hendes breve","Gennem en samtale med en ven"],"a":"Gennem det, hun gør","r":"Forfatteren viser ensomheden indirekte gennem Annas handlinger: hun dækker bord til to, selv om hun bor alene."},
{"l":9590,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Historians once assumed that the Vikings never reached North America. Excavations in Newfoundland, however, proved them wrong.' Hvad viser teksten?","o":["At vikingerne aldrig kom til Amerika","At en tidligere antagelse blev modbevist","At historikere altid har haft ret","At udgravningerne intet fandt"],"a":"At en tidligere antagelse blev modbevist","r":"'Once assumed' og 'proved them wrong' viser, at en gammel antagelse blev modbevist af udgravningerne."},
{"l":9620,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Passengers are kindly requested to ___ from smoking on board.'","o":["prevent","resist","refrain","stop"],"a":"refrain","r":"'Refrain from' er et formelt udtryk for at afholde sig fra noget. De andre verber kan ikke stå med 'from' på denne måde."},
{"l":9640,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The bridge is thought ___ in the twelfth century.'","o":["to be built","having been built","to build","to have been built"],"a":"to have been built","r":"Broen blev bygget i fortiden og er passiv, så man bruger perfektum-passiv infinitiv: 'to have been built'."},
{"l":9680,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'well under way' i 'Preparations for the school festival are already well under way.'?","o":["i fuld gang","helt forsinkede","næsten aflyste","slet ikke startet"],"a":"i fuld gang","r":"'Well under way' betyder, at noget allerede er godt i gang."},
{"l":9700,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The coach insisted that every player ___ on time for training.'","o":["being","be","to be","been"],"a":"be","r":"Efter 'insist that' kan man bruge konjunktiv: grundformen 'be' uden endelse. 'To be' og 'being' kan ikke stå efter 'that'."},
{"l":9720,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man afslutter et formelt brev, der begyndte uden modtagerens navn?","o":["Lots of love","Take care","Yours faithfully","See you around"],"a":"Yours faithfully","r":"I britisk engelsk afslutter man et formelt brev til en ukendt modtager med 'Yours faithfully'. De andre er uformelle."},
{"l":9740,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The instructions claimed the shelf could be assembled in ten minutes. Three hours, two broken screws and one very long phone call later, it was finally standing.' Hvad antyder skribenten?","o":["At reolen var hurtig og nem at samle","At skribenten havde mistet vejledningen","At telefonen gik i stykker undervejs","At vejledningen var alt for optimistisk"],"a":"At vejledningen var alt for optimistisk","r":"'Claimed' og kontrasten mellem ti minutter og tre timer viser, at vejledningens løfte var urealistisk."},
{"l":9770,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The two classes have a ___ rivalry that goes back many years.'","o":["long-standing","outstanding","freestanding","notwithstanding"],"a":"long-standing","r":"'Long-standing' betyder langvarig, som har eksisteret længe. 'Outstanding' betyder fremragende eller udestående."},
{"l":9800,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The museum guide spoke so quietly that, by the end of the tour, most of the group had drifted off to look at the paintings on their own.' Hvad kan man udlede af teksten?","o":["Guiden var vred på gruppen","De fleste kunne ikke høre guiden ordentligt","Gruppen interesserede sig ikke for malerier","Rundvisningen sluttede alt for tidligt"],"a":"De fleste kunne ikke høre guiden ordentligt","r":"Guiden talte så lavt, at gruppen gled væk og kiggede selv; man kan udlede, at de ikke kunne høre hende."},
{"l":9820,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Pupils must ___ a balance between schoolwork and free time.'","o":["make","hit","strike","beat"],"a":"strike","r":"Den faste forbindelse er 'strike a balance' (finde den rette balance)."},
{"l":9850,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Every single one of the eggs survived the drop, which is more than can be said for Mr Hansen and his lab coat.' Hvad kan man udlede af teksten?","o":["At alle æggene gik i stykker til sidst","At læreren fik en ny kittel af klassen","At forsøget blev aflyst på grund af ham","At det gik værre for læreren end for æggene"],"a":"At det gik værre for læreren end for æggene","r":"'Which is more than can be said for' betyder, at det samme ikke gjaldt for hr. Hansen og hans kittel; han klarede sig dårligere end æggene."},
{"l":9880,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'gregarious' i 'a gregarious person'?","o":["sociable","generous","stubborn","gorgeous"],"a":"sociable","r":"'Gregarious' betyder selskabelig og glad for andres selskab, altså 'sociable'."},
{"l":9900,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'concur' i 'concur with the expert'?","o":["argue","agree","compete","consult"],"a":"agree","r":"'Concur' er et formelt ord for at være enig, altså 'agree'."},
{"l":9950,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'precarious' i 'The climber found himself in a precarious position on the narrow ledge.'?","o":["behagelig","ensom","farefuld","heldig"],"a":"farefuld","r":"'Precarious' betyder usikker og farefuld; klatreren stod på en smal afsats."},
{"l":9970,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Not that I am complaining, but this is the third time this month that my order has arrived broken.' Hvad er skribentens egentlige hensigt?","o":["At rose den hurtige levering","At bestille noget nyt hos firmaet","At takke for en god service","At klage, selv om det nægtes"],"a":"At klage, selv om det nægtes","r":"'Not that I am complaining, but' indleder typisk netop en klage; skribenten klager over ødelagte varer."},
{"l":9990,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'While the new app is undeniably convenient, one cannot help wondering how much of our personal data it quietly collects.' Hvilken holdning har skribenten til appen?","o":["Positiv, men også skeptisk","Udelukkende begejstret","Helt ligeglad","Meget vred"],"a":"Positiv, men også skeptisk","r":"'Undeniably convenient' er positivt, men 'cannot help wondering' viser skepsis over for dataindsamlingen."},
{"l":10000,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'stille op over for hinanden' på engelsk?","o":["transpose","juxtapose","expose","propose"],"a":"juxtapose","r":"'Juxtapose' = sidestille for at vise kontrast."}
]$$::jsonb) AS e
JOIN (VALUES
  ('o', 'ordforråd', 'recall', 'factual', 'surface_association'),
  ('h', 'hverdagsudtryk', 'comprehension', 'conceptual', 'surface_association'),
  ('g', 'grammatik', 'application', 'applied', 'overgeneralization'),
  ('l', 'læseforståelse', 'analysis', 'inferential', 'surface_association')
) AS m(k, concept, skill, dtype, mis) ON m.k = e->>'k';
